    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255-a1">

                <pb facs="0423" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg327"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. H. Johnson to Mr. Turner.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia,
                                Liberia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 28,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint your
                    excellency that the sovereign people of Liberia having, on the 26th day of the
                    present month, deposed President Roye, the government of Liberia will be
                    provisionally conducted by a chief executive committee and the chiefs of
                    departments, until the arrival at the government of the vice-president of the
                    republic.</p>
                <p>I beg to inclose herein a copy of the manifesto issued by the provisional
                    government under date of October 27, instant.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. R. W. JOHNSON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
